---
/**
 * `/accessibility` — DRAFT for attorney review.
 *
 * Two halves, and the second is the one that matters: this website, and the
 * building. The building is not step-free anywhere, and saying so plainly is both
 * required and more useful than a statement of commitment.
 *
 * Describes the building. Never the reader. COMPLIANCE.md bans "must be able to"
 * and "able bodied" — a capability requirement in a housing advert is a disability
 * problem, and a warning about who "should" apply is exactly that.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, home } from '../data/site.config';
const updated = '27 July 2026';
---
<Base title="Accessibility" description="How accessible this website is, and how accessible the building is.">
  <section class="wrap stack measure">
    <h1 class="display-l">Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="draft"><strong>Draft, pending legal review.</strong> Last updated {updated}.</p>

    <h2>The building</h2>
    <p class="hard">
      <strong>There is no step-free route into this house, or to any bedroom.</strong>
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>{home.entry.front}</li>
      <li>{home.entry.back}</li>
      <li>Every bedroom is on the second or third floor.</li>
      <li>The house is stairs only. There is no lift.</li>
      
    </ul>
    <p>
      We would rather you learn this here than on arrival. If you are weighing whether the building
      works for you, call {site.contact.phone} and ask — we will describe it honestly and in detail
      rather than guess on your behalf.
    </p>

    <h2>Reasonable accommodations</h2>
    <p>
      If a disability means you need something different — a change to a rule, a practice, or a
      physical feature — ask. Requests are considered on their facts and are not put to a vote of other
      residents.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Service animals and assistance animals are not pets.</strong>
      {' '}{home.pets.assistanceAnimalCarveOut}
    </p>
    <p>Requests go to {site.contact.name} at {site.contact.email} or {site.contact.phone}.</p>

    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>We aim to meet WCAG 2.1 Level AA. What is deliberately true of this site today:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Every page works with JavaScript turned off.</li>
      <li>Every interactive control is reachable and operable by keyboard, with a visible focus ring.</li>
      <li>Text contrast was audited against the background it actually sits on, not assumed.</li>
      <li>Images carry real alternative text describing what they show.</li>
      <li>Content is structured with real headings, lists and tables rather than styled text.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Known gaps: the embedded map on the commute page is a third-party Google frame we do not control,
      so the distances and drive times are given as text above it and the page does not depend on the
      map.
    </p>

    <h2>Telling us something is wrong</h2>
    <p>
      If any part of this site or this building is difficult to use, tell us at {site.contact.email} or
      {site.contact.phone}. Say what you were trying to do and what happened. We will reply
      {' '}{site.response.commitment}.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
<style>
  section { padding-block: var(--s12) var(--s8); }
  .draft { border-left: 3px solid var(--brick); padding-left: var(--s4); }
  .hard { border-left: 3px solid var(--signal); padding-left: var(--s4); font-size: 1.125rem; }
  h2 { margin-top: var(--s8); }
  ul { padding-left: var(--s6); }
  li + li { margin-top: var(--s2); }
</style>
